  <description>
    <p>Evaluates a polynomial with constant Coefficients (highest power first).</p>
    <table border="1">
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Module</td><td><code>nflow_blocks</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Library</td><td>Math</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Type</td><td><code>polynomial</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Label</td><td>Polynomial</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p><img src="../../../../libraries/math/exports/polynomial.svg" align="middle"/></p>
    <p><b>Description</b></p>
    <p>Evaluates a polynomial with constant <code>Coefficients</code> (highest power first, polyval order) at the input using Horner's method. For Coefficients = [a b c], out = a*u^2 + b*u + c. Pure algebraic feedthrough, element-wise; the Horner form is unrolled over the static coefficients in generated code.</p>
    <p><b>Ports</b></p>
    <p><b>Input(s)</b></p>
    <table border="1">
      <thead><tr><th>Port</th><th>Role</th><th>Side</th><th>Position</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Port_1</td><td>Numeric signal read by the block.</td><td>left</td><td>x=0, y=40</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p><b>Output(s)</b></p>
    <table border="1">
      <thead><tr><th>Port</th><th>Role</th><th>Side</th><th>Position</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Port_1</td><td>Numeric signal produced by the block.</td><td>right</td><td>x=80, y=40</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p><b>Parameters</b></p>
    <table border="1">
      <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Default value</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>Coefficients</code></td><td>[1 0 0]</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p><b>Block Characteristics</b></p>
    <table border="1">
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Block type</td><td>polynomial</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Family</td><td>Math</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Rendered size</td><td>80 x 80</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Phases</td><td>ALGEBRAIC</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Internal state or history</td><td>no</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Signal data type</td><td>double numeric values</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p><b>Algorithms</b></p>
    <ul>
      <li>ALGEBRAIC: Horner evaluation acc = c[0]; acc = acc*u + c[k] for k = 1..n-1.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><b>Equation or Rule</b></p>
    <latex>y = \sum_{k=0}^{n-1} c_k\, u^{\,n-1-k}</latex>
    <p><b>Extended Capabilities</b></p>
    <p>Code generation: supported for C and Rust.</p>
